---
// Privacy Notice (DPDP Act, 2023). DRAFT: items in [square brackets] are company facts that VK
// Solar must confirm; they are shown as-is rather than guessed. Have it reviewed before launch.
import SiteLayout from '../layouts/SiteLayout.astro';
import PageHero from '../components/PageHero.astro';
import { site, businessOf } from '../config/site';

const business = businessOf(Astro.locals);
const contactEmail = business.contact.email ?? '[privacy contact email]';
const contactPhone = business.contact.phoneDisplay ?? business.contact.phone ?? '[phone number]';
const address = business.contact.address ?? '[registered office address]';
---

<SiteLayout title="Privacy Notice" description={`How ${site.shortName} collects, uses and protects your personal data, and the rights you have under India's Digital Personal Data Protection Act, 2023.`}>
  <PageHero eyebrow="Privacy" title="Privacy Notice">
    <p>How we collect, use and protect your personal data. Last updated: [date].</p>
  </PageHero>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container privacy">
      <p>
        This notice explains how <strong>[full registered legal name of VK Solar]</strong> (“{site.shortName}”, “we”, “us”) collects and uses your
        personal data when you use this website, including our contact form and customer account. We process personal data in line with the Digital
        Personal Data Protection Act, 2023.
      </p>

      <h2>1. Who is responsible for your data</h2>
      <p>{site.shortName} is the Data Fiduciary for personal data collected through this website.</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Registered address: <span class="privacy__lines">{address}</span></li>
        <li>Privacy questions and grievances: [name or role of the responsible person], {contactEmail}, {contactPhone}</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>2. What personal data we collect</h2>
      <h3>When you send an enquiry through the contact form</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>Your name and phone number, and your email address if you give it.</li>
        <li>The service you are interested in, your state or union territory, and your site location.</li>
        <li>Any message you write, and a record that you agreed to be contacted and when.</li>
      </ul>
      <h3>When you create a customer account</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>Your name, email address and phone number, and optionally your city or town and state.</li>
        <li>A record that you accepted this notice, and when.</li>
        <li>Your password, which is handled by our authentication provider (Google Firebase Authentication). We never see or store your password.</li>
      </ul>
      <h3>When you request a service through your account</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>The service requested, site location, state, system size (if given) and any details you add.</li>
        <li>The status of each request and when it changed.</li>
        <li>Internal notes our staff add to manage your request, used only internally.</li>
      </ul>
      <h3>Technical data</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>
          Cookies: we use only cookies that are strictly necessary for the website to work — a sign-in cookie that keeps you logged in (up to 5 days)
          and short-lived security cookies that protect our forms against misuse. We do not use advertising, analytics or tracking cookies.
        </li>
        <li>
          Your internet (IP) address is used temporarily to prevent abuse, such as too many sign-in attempts or form submissions. It is not stored with
          your enquiry or account.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p>We do not ask for, and ask you not to send, sensitive information such as financial details, identity numbers or health information.</p>

      <h2>3. Why we use your data</h2>
      <ol>
        <li>To respond to your enquiry and contact you about it by phone or email.</li>
        <li>To create and manage your customer account.</li>
        <li>To receive, schedule, carry out and update you on the services you request.</li>
        <li>To keep the website secure and prevent misuse.</li>
        <li>To meet our legal obligations.</li>
      </ol>
      <p>
        We do not sell your personal data or use it for advertising. We process it on the basis of your consent, which you give when you submit the
        contact form or create an account. You can withdraw it at any time (see section 7).
      </p>

      <h2>4. Who we share it with</h2>
      <p>We share personal data only with service providers who help us run the website, and only as needed:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Google (Firebase Authentication and Cloud Firestore), to manage customer accounts and store account and request data, in [Google Cloud region].</li>
        <li>Our email provider ([provider]), to send internal notifications about new enquiries, if enabled.</li>
        <li>Our hosting provider ([provider]), which runs the website.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>Some providers may process data outside India, as permitted under the DPDP Act. We may also disclose data where the law requires it.</p>

      <h2>5. How long we keep it</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Enquiries are kept while we deal with them and deleted [365 days] after they are resolved, unless the law requires us to keep them longer.</li>
        <li>Customer accounts are kept until you ask us to delete them. Service requests are kept for [period].</li>
        <li>Backups may contain copies of your data for a limited time and are overwritten in the normal course.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>6. How we protect it</h2>
      <p>
        Only authorised staff can see your data, through a protected admin area. Data is encrypted in transit (HTTPS). Passwords are handled by Google
        Firebase Authentication. Customers can only see their own account and requests.
      </p>

      <h2>7. Your rights</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Access a summary of the personal data we hold about you and how we use it.</li>
        <li>Correct, complete or update your data — you can edit your profile in your account, or contact us.</li>
        <li>Erase your data or delete your account by contacting us at {contactEmail}.</li>
        <li>Withdraw your consent at any time, as easily as you gave it. This does not affect processing already done, but we may no longer be able to provide the service.</li>
        <li>Nominate another person to exercise these rights if you die or become incapable.</li>
        <li>Raise a grievance with us. We will respond within [30 days]. If you are not satisfied, you may complain to the Data Protection Board of India.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>To exercise these rights, contact [name or role] at {contactEmail}. We may ask you to confirm your identity first.</p>

      <h2>8. Children</h2>
      <p>This website and its services are for adults (18 or over). If you are under 18, please do not create an account or send us your details.</p>

      <h2>9. Changes to this notice</h2>
      <p>We may update this notice; the date above shows the latest version. If a change significantly affects how we use your data, we will tell you on the website or by email.</p>

      <h2>10. Contact us</h2>
      <p>[full registered legal name] · <span class="privacy__lines">{address}</span> · {contactEmail} · {contactPhone}</p>
    </div>
  </section>
</SiteLayout>

<style>
  .privacy {
    max-width: 72ch;
  }

  .privacy h2 {
    margin-top: var(--space-5);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-1-5);
    font-size: var(--fs-h3);
  }

  .privacy h3 {
    margin-top: var(--space-3);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-1);
    font-size: var(--fs-h4);
  }

  .privacy p,
  .privacy li {
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    overflow-wrap: anywhere;
  }

  .privacy ul,
  .privacy ol {
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--space-1);
    padding-left: var(--space-3);
  }

  .privacy ul {
    list-style: disc;
  }

  .privacy ol {
    list-style: decimal;
  }

  .privacy p + p,
  .privacy ul + p,
  .privacy ol + p {
    margin-top: var(--space-1-5);
  }

  .privacy__lines {
    white-space: pre-line;
  }
</style>
